1
00:00:02,302 --> 00:00:05,239
EPISODE 8

2
00:00:31,598 --> 00:00:34,635
Jeez, drinking again?

3
00:00:38,305 --> 00:00:40,073
Why? Did something happen again?

4
00:00:53,654 --> 00:00:55,989
-Pour me a glass too.
-You too?

5
00:00:59,426 --> 00:01:02,930
Why? Thinking about that girl,
Yu-na or Yu-ja, again?

6
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,404
I'm saying this
because I really care about you.

7
00:01:11,672 --> 00:01:13,206
Just give it up now.

8
00:01:14,141 --> 00:01:17,477
I haven't lived that long,
but from what I've seen in life,

9
00:01:17,544 --> 00:01:21,315
getting your hopes up won't make
something impossible work out.

10
00:01:21,381 --> 00:01:23,050
It just doesn't work that way.

11
00:01:26,954 --> 00:01:28,589
I don't care

12
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:33,694
whether she looks my way or not.

13
00:01:36,597 --> 00:01:39,733
Though she's in a glamorous place
far above me,

14
00:01:42,502 --> 00:01:44,471
to me, Yu-na is always…

15
00:01:45,906 --> 00:01:47,574
someone I feel for,

16
00:01:48,642 --> 00:01:50,277
someone my heart aches for,

17
00:01:52,746 --> 00:01:54,481
and someone I want to protect.

18
00:01:56,583 --> 00:01:58,986
I don't know if I'll ever reach her,

19
00:01:59,586 --> 00:02:02,322
but if I can, I want to protect her.

20
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:11,131
Once a man makes up his mind,
he covers the after-sales service too.

21
00:02:22,209 --> 00:02:25,946
Sang-eun, sir! Sir!

22
00:02:26,013 --> 00:02:27,648
Man-gu!

23
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:30,951
What on earth is going on?

24
00:02:32,686 --> 00:02:35,288
Man-gu, what happened here?

25
00:02:38,458 --> 00:02:43,063
I came out this morning and saw
some bastards wiped it all out.

26
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:46,600
What kind of bastards
would do something like this?

27
00:02:55,742 --> 00:02:59,146
We kept quiet, but I heard
our apple orchard got robbed too.

28
00:02:59,212 --> 00:03:01,214
Is that true?

29
00:03:05,819 --> 00:03:07,254
Uncle, what's wrong?

30
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:11,491
Some bastards just wiped out
our entire sweet potato field.

31
00:03:11,558 --> 00:03:15,062
I just went to the field,
and it's in total chaos!

32
00:03:15,128 --> 00:03:16,863
Your field too?

33
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:19,666
This looks like the work
of professional thieves.

34
00:03:19,733 --> 00:03:22,869
I think we should come up with a plan.

35
00:03:22,936 --> 00:03:27,007
We were busy eating fried soybeans
and didn't even plant the seedlings.

36
00:03:27,074 --> 00:03:28,675
But aren't they so good?

37
00:03:28,742 --> 00:03:31,978
I never get tired of these.
They're totally addictive.

38
00:03:32,879 --> 00:03:34,514
Oh? Sir!

39
00:03:35,816 --> 00:03:36,950
What's he doing?

40
00:03:37,017 --> 00:03:38,685
What are you doing here, sir?

41
00:03:42,289 --> 00:03:46,126
I heard the ginseng field was robbed,
and this mess is no joke.

42
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:49,062
That must be a huge loss.

43
00:03:49,129 --> 00:03:51,498
The loss is one thing, but

44
00:03:52,466 --> 00:03:55,936
I feel empty without the little guys
I watched for three years.

45
00:03:57,137 --> 00:04:00,107
After work, I'd tell them
good night and head home.

46
00:04:00,173 --> 00:04:03,677
In the morning, I'd come ask
if they'd slept well,

47
00:04:03,744 --> 00:04:06,179
and we'd have cozy little chats.

48
00:04:06,246 --> 00:04:08,849
In the summer, I pulled their weeds.

49
00:04:08,915 --> 00:04:10,383
Winter gets cold, you know,

50
00:04:11,051 --> 00:04:13,019
so I covered them with blankets too.

51
00:04:13,086 --> 00:04:16,189
I cared for them more than my own kids.

52
00:04:19,025 --> 00:04:22,295
Gosh, I'm making a fool of myself.

53
00:04:23,196 --> 00:04:24,664
Sir.

54
00:04:26,366 --> 00:04:27,400
Please stay strong.

55
00:04:27,467 --> 00:04:29,102
You all go on ahead.

56
00:04:29,169 --> 00:04:30,904
I'll stay a little longer.

57
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:34,708
We're back!

58
00:04:34,775 --> 00:04:36,176
-We're back.
-Okay.

59
00:04:36,243 --> 00:04:37,611
You're back?

60
00:04:37,677 --> 00:04:39,012
What are you doing?

61
00:04:39,846 --> 00:04:42,482
I'm assigning teams
for our village patrol tonight.

62
00:04:42,549 --> 00:04:43,416
A patrol?

63
00:04:43,483 --> 00:04:46,620
You know Man-gu's ginseng field
got robbed last night?

64
00:04:46,686 --> 00:04:48,922
Yes, we ran into him on the way here.

65
00:04:48,989 --> 00:04:52,259
And I heard In-gi's apple orchard
got robbed recently too.

66
00:04:52,325 --> 00:04:54,327
That's not all.

67
00:04:54,394 --> 00:04:58,865
That thief completely cleaned out
our sweet potato field too!

68
00:04:58,932 --> 00:05:00,667
Sweet potatoes too?

69
00:05:00,734 --> 00:05:02,669
Why steal them? They're so cheap.

70
00:05:02,736 --> 00:05:04,738
That's what I'm saying!

71
00:05:04,805 --> 00:05:09,309
And seeing how one footprint is big
and the other one is small,

72
00:05:09,376 --> 00:05:12,846
it's definitely a mixed duo
of male and female thieves.

73
00:05:14,581 --> 00:05:16,917
A mixed duo?
What kind of sweet potatoes?

74
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,652
-Chestnut ones.
-Chestnut ones!

75
00:05:19,953 --> 00:05:21,855
Why are you so startled?

76
00:05:21,922 --> 00:05:24,291
Because of a bug. It's nothing.

77
00:05:24,357 --> 00:05:28,228
Whoever that punk is,
if I ever get my hands on him,

78
00:05:28,295 --> 00:05:30,831
I'll snap his back right in half!

79
00:05:30,897 --> 00:05:32,332
That little bastard!

80
00:05:32,399 --> 00:05:34,000
Uncle, please calm down.

81
00:05:34,901 --> 00:05:39,039
But this really looks like the work
of professional crop thieves.

82
00:05:39,105 --> 00:05:41,942
So starting tonight,
we're all patrolling all night.

83
00:05:42,008 --> 00:05:43,810
Don't even think of sleep, got it?

84
00:05:43,877 --> 00:05:45,111
-Yes.
-Good.

85
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:46,479
-Give me Team 4.
-Team 4?

86
00:05:47,948 --> 00:05:49,950
Su-yeon wouldn't know about this.

87
00:05:50,016 --> 00:05:51,852
Surely she won't go again today?

88
00:05:52,586 --> 00:05:54,254
That can't happen.

89
00:05:58,658 --> 00:06:00,293
-Where are you going?
-Huh?

90
00:06:01,027 --> 00:06:02,829
For a walk. Just a walk.

91
00:06:02,896 --> 00:06:04,998
The air is so fresh!

92
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:09,836
Su-yeon! Su-yeon!

93
00:06:10,670 --> 00:06:12,572
Sir, is Su-yeon inside?

94
00:06:12,639 --> 00:06:15,508
Su-yeon? She went out earlier.

95
00:06:15,575 --> 00:06:17,010
Already? Where to?

96
00:06:17,077 --> 00:06:18,879
I wouldn't know that.

97
00:06:18,945 --> 00:06:22,282
She left saying not to wait up
since she might be late.

98
00:06:22,349 --> 00:06:25,752
Where could she have gone this early?

99
00:06:26,519 --> 00:06:29,656
-Want some peanuts?
-Thank you, sir.

100
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:31,691
Is she raiding crops again?

101
00:06:32,559 --> 00:06:33,860
Nah, couldn't be.

102
00:06:36,930 --> 00:06:38,999
Wow, these peanuts taste amazing!

103
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:40,667
You dug these up today, sir?

104
00:06:40,734 --> 00:06:45,138
As I said last time, my teeth are bad.

105
00:06:48,942 --> 00:06:51,077
Seriously, sir, why do this to me?

106
00:06:51,144 --> 00:06:54,180
Just throw them away!
Why are you drying them?

107
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,248
It'd be a waste.

108
00:06:55,315 --> 00:06:57,651
Yuck, seriously! Ptui!

109
00:06:57,717 --> 00:07:02,188
Where did Su-yeon go again?
Raiding crops today means big trouble.

110
00:07:02,255 --> 00:07:03,690
I'll be going now, sir.

111
00:07:03,757 --> 00:07:06,559
Just toss them out already! Seriously!

112
00:07:08,295 --> 00:07:09,963
Those dirty thieving bastards!

113
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:11,431
Wait till I catch them!

114
00:07:11,498 --> 00:07:13,300
I know. Of all things to steal,

115
00:07:13,366 --> 00:07:15,568
why crops we sweated over all year?

116
00:07:15,635 --> 00:07:17,671
Han-cheol said he was coming.

117
00:07:17,737 --> 00:07:19,272
Where did he go?

118
00:07:19,339 --> 00:07:22,609
Since we're on patrol,
he's definitely holed up somewhere.

119
00:07:22,676 --> 00:07:24,744
You think so? Seriously.

120
00:07:24,811 --> 00:07:26,780
Wait, hold on.

121
00:07:26,846 --> 00:07:29,716
I told you two not to tag along.

122
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:30,884
Why keep following?

123
00:07:30,951 --> 00:07:32,752
We should help the village too.

124
00:07:33,420 --> 00:07:36,856
Right. Does gender matter for this?

125
00:07:36,923 --> 00:07:40,860
Oh, but since it's so dark…

126
00:07:41,594 --> 00:07:43,363
I'm scared.

127
00:07:43,930 --> 00:07:46,199
-What's this?
-Tell me about it.

128
00:07:46,266 --> 00:07:48,301
I'm so scared too.

129
00:07:50,437 --> 00:07:52,672
Hey, what are you two doing?

130
00:07:52,739 --> 00:07:55,342
-Min-gi, I'm scared too.
-Want to die?

131
00:07:55,408 --> 00:07:56,576
-Let's go.

132
00:07:57,978 --> 00:08:00,180
-Sort it out and come on.
-Hey, wait up!

133
00:08:00,246 --> 00:08:02,615
-Hyeok, I'm scared.
-Hey, I'm more scared!

134
00:08:02,682 --> 00:08:06,720
Goodness, what a hassle every harvest.

135
00:08:06,786 --> 00:08:09,422
Whoever those punks are,
wait till I catch them!

136
00:08:09,489 --> 00:08:11,491
I'll tear them to pieces!

137
00:08:11,558 --> 00:08:13,126
By the way, Sang-deuk.

138
00:08:13,193 --> 00:08:15,895
Shouldn't we each carry a club?

139
00:08:15,962 --> 00:08:17,464
You're right.

140
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:19,966
I'll get some, so please go on ahead.

141
00:08:20,033 --> 00:08:21,234
Okay, sounds good.

142
00:08:21,301 --> 00:08:24,070
While you're at it, get a hefty one.

143
00:08:24,137 --> 00:08:25,638
Just one hit from it, huh?

144
00:08:25,705 --> 00:08:27,240
Blood dripping, whack, bam!

145
00:08:27,307 --> 00:08:29,175
So guts slide out like fish cake?

146
00:08:29,242 --> 00:08:30,844
Yes, don't worry.

147
00:08:31,945 --> 00:08:33,013
Let's go, ma'am.

148
00:08:33,079 --> 00:08:34,714
Those damn bastards.

149
00:08:40,787 --> 00:08:42,188
Perfect, just perfect.

150
00:08:43,556 --> 00:08:46,326
Darn it, this really won't come out.

151
00:08:46,393 --> 00:08:47,694
Huh?

152
00:08:47,761 --> 00:08:48,895
Gosh.

153
00:08:50,130 --> 00:08:51,998
Who's there? Jeez, who are you?

154
00:08:52,065 --> 00:08:53,933
Sang-deuk! It's me, Mi-yeong!

155
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:57,303
I was just stretching. You scared me.

156
00:08:58,538 --> 00:09:01,708
Why are you out at this hour
instead of sleeping?

157
00:09:01,775 --> 00:09:04,310
I just wanted to take a walk.

158
00:09:05,512 --> 00:09:08,982
Thieves are out prowling.
Stop fooling around and go inside.

159
00:09:09,049 --> 00:09:12,852
Um, Sang-deuk, I have something to say.

160
00:09:12,919 --> 00:09:15,021
Something to say? Like what?

161
00:09:17,157 --> 00:09:18,892
Um, the thing is…

162
00:09:21,761 --> 00:09:24,464
I haven't lived like nothing happened.

163
00:09:26,466 --> 00:09:28,668
Since I broke up with you like that,

164
00:09:29,969 --> 00:09:33,206
I haven't slept easy for a single day.

165
00:09:34,808 --> 00:09:37,377
I never should've done that to you.

166
00:09:38,812 --> 00:09:42,882
I guess I was punished for it.
I even got divorced.

167
00:09:45,051 --> 00:09:47,153
And my dad is sick too.

168
00:09:50,156 --> 00:09:53,893
Today, I have to tell you
what I couldn't say for 17 years.

169
00:09:55,829 --> 00:09:56,863
Sang-deuk…

170
00:09:58,832 --> 00:10:00,166
I'm sorry.

171
00:10:01,768 --> 00:10:03,703
I'm so sorry.

172
00:10:05,472 --> 00:10:07,640
It was my fault.

173
00:10:10,410 --> 00:10:12,479
Don't cry.

174
00:10:12,545 --> 00:10:14,514
What's crying going to change?

175
00:10:15,248 --> 00:10:17,550
I'm sorry, Sang-deuk.

176
00:10:18,451 --> 00:10:19,519
Oh, gosh.

177
00:10:26,392 --> 00:10:28,695
Oh! Mom!

178
00:10:28,761 --> 00:10:30,497
This is bad. Hurry, go!

179
00:10:34,334 --> 00:10:35,435
I'm so sorry.

180
00:10:35,502 --> 00:10:38,104
I think I forgot to turn off the gas.

181
00:10:38,171 --> 00:10:39,506
That's all right.

182
00:10:39,572 --> 00:10:42,208
You can go on alone from here, right?

183
00:10:42,275 --> 00:10:44,944
I have an urgent phone call to make.

184
00:10:45,011 --> 00:10:46,045
Of course.

185
00:10:46,112 --> 00:10:47,413
My house is right here.

186
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:49,883
Then please take this flashlight.

187
00:10:49,949 --> 00:10:51,484
Thank you.

188
00:10:51,551 --> 00:10:53,686
-Take care.
-Yes, you too.

189
00:10:56,990 --> 00:10:58,158
Phew.

190
00:10:58,224 --> 00:11:00,160
Gosh, that was a close call.

191
00:11:12,205 --> 00:11:14,340
Jeez, it smells like pee.

192
00:11:20,346 --> 00:11:22,282
Su-yeon!

193
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:25,185
I swear, where did she go again?

194
00:11:26,653 --> 00:11:28,354
Su-yeon!

195
00:11:29,322 --> 00:11:30,623
Su-yeon…

196
00:11:33,259 --> 00:11:35,862
What is she doing over there again?

197
00:11:35,929 --> 00:11:37,230
I swear, Su-yeon.

198
00:11:38,164 --> 00:11:39,399
Su-yeon.

199
00:11:40,934 --> 00:11:43,203
What are you doing here right now?

200
00:11:43,269 --> 00:11:46,072
No way, are you swiping
sweet potatoes again?

201
00:11:46,139 --> 00:11:48,074
Huh? Yes.

202
00:11:48,141 --> 00:11:50,443
Are you crazy about sweet potatoes?

203
00:11:50,510 --> 00:11:52,845
You dug up plenty yesterday.

204
00:11:52,912 --> 00:11:54,981
Why are you being so greedy, really?

205
00:11:55,048 --> 00:11:57,550
-Well, um…
-Forget it, just forget it.

206
00:11:57,617 --> 00:11:59,519
Now is not the time for this.

207
00:11:59,586 --> 00:12:01,554
We're in big trouble if we're caught…

208
00:12:01,621 --> 00:12:03,590
Hold on, I think I heard something.

209
00:12:06,059 --> 00:12:09,062
Who's there! Who's out there!

210
00:12:09,128 --> 00:12:10,730
Is someone out there?

211
00:12:14,300 --> 00:12:16,035
Nobody's out there.

212
00:12:16,102 --> 00:12:19,172
Strange. I definitely heard something.

213
00:12:19,239 --> 00:12:21,608
You must've heard wrong. Let's go.

214
00:12:29,515 --> 00:12:30,550
Did you hear that?

215
00:12:32,452 --> 00:12:36,022
Who's there! Which bastard is it?
Come out right now!

216
00:12:36,089 --> 00:12:39,158
Fine, so Your Highnesses
won't come out, is that it?

217
00:12:39,225 --> 00:12:41,327
Then we'll come to you.

218
00:12:41,394 --> 00:12:43,963
You're dead meat today,
you thieving bastards!

219
00:12:48,735 --> 00:12:50,670
Oh, no! Mr. Man-gu!

220
00:12:50,737 --> 00:12:52,839
Oh, it's me! It's just me, see?

221
00:12:52,905 --> 00:12:54,607
Mr. Man-gu!

222
00:12:54,674 --> 00:12:57,443
Mr. Man-gu! Goodness, this is…

223
00:12:57,510 --> 00:13:00,513
Mr. Man-gu! It's me, sir!

224
00:13:02,348 --> 00:13:04,250
What? Han-cheol, is that you?

225
00:13:04,317 --> 00:13:07,420
Ding, ding, ding! Yes, I am Han-cheol!

226
00:13:08,087 --> 00:13:10,290
What are you doing here right now?

227
00:13:12,225 --> 00:13:14,727
Were you just stealing sweet potatoes?

228
00:13:16,929 --> 00:13:18,831
I wasn't stealing them.

229
00:13:18,898 --> 00:13:20,500
I was foraging, just foraging.

230
00:13:20,566 --> 00:13:24,904
What? Is this guy out of his mind?

231
00:13:24,971 --> 00:13:28,474
Don't tell me you hit Yeong-sik's
sweet potato field too?

232
00:13:28,541 --> 00:13:30,209
Yes, I did it.

233
00:13:30,276 --> 00:13:32,145
I did it all by myself!

234
00:13:32,211 --> 00:13:34,947
I'm really crazy about
sweet potatoes, just crazy!

235
00:13:36,916 --> 00:13:38,785
Mmm, it's good.

236
00:13:43,956 --> 00:13:46,025
-Wait!
-Is this guy out of his mind?

237
00:13:46,092 --> 00:13:47,327
-Hold on!
-Follow me.

238
00:13:47,393 --> 00:13:49,595
-You little punk!
-Wait a second!

239
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,264
Sweet potatoes are so cheap!

240
00:14:07,347 --> 00:14:09,248
I wonder if the patrol's going well.

241
00:14:09,916 --> 00:14:11,017
I can't go out with this leg.

242
00:14:11,084 --> 00:14:12,118
PIANIST LEE HYEON-SEOK

243
00:14:13,019 --> 00:14:14,253
-Oh, my.
-Hello.

244
00:14:14,320 --> 00:14:17,357
How can a pianist be that handsome?

245
00:14:17,423 --> 00:14:19,959
He just oozes class and elegance.

246
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:22,295
How do you feel?

247
00:14:22,362 --> 00:14:24,230
I still have a long way to go.

248
00:14:24,297 --> 00:14:25,965
Making the top ten like this

249
00:14:26,032 --> 00:14:29,969
is a true honor, and I am so grateful.

250
00:14:31,137 --> 00:14:33,206
What? What's wrong? I was watching!

251
00:14:33,272 --> 00:14:34,440
Kang Min-ho, bed now.

252
00:14:34,507 --> 00:14:35,475
It's past bedtime.

253
00:14:35,541 --> 00:14:37,310
But I'm not sleepy yet.

254
00:14:37,377 --> 00:14:39,479
Go to sleep! Want to get in trouble?

255
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:42,215
Why are you yelling at him like that?

256
00:14:42,281 --> 00:14:46,185
Min-ho, sleep with Great-Aunt tonight.

257
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:58,197
Sis.

258
00:14:58,865 --> 00:15:00,700
That man earlier was him, right?

259
00:15:00,767 --> 00:15:02,602
What are you saying? What man?

260
00:15:02,668 --> 00:15:04,103
I remember everything.

261
00:15:04,871 --> 00:15:06,873
-It was him, wasn't it?
-Stop it.

262
00:15:08,107 --> 00:15:09,909
Don't tell anyone about this.

263
00:15:09,976 --> 00:15:11,444
If you do,

264
00:15:12,245 --> 00:15:14,447
I swear, as your sister,

265
00:15:14,514 --> 00:15:16,816
I'll get really mad at you.

266
00:15:16,883 --> 00:15:18,518
Got it?

267
00:15:39,872 --> 00:15:41,174
What are you doing?

268
00:15:43,409 --> 00:15:44,677
Nothing.

269
00:15:44,744 --> 00:15:47,079
I felt suffocated just sitting still.

270
00:15:47,146 --> 00:15:49,282
So I'm taking this out on patrol.

271
00:15:50,683 --> 00:15:52,618
Patrol, my foot. Not with that leg.

272
00:15:59,025 --> 00:16:00,960
What's with the look on your face?

273
00:16:02,428 --> 00:16:04,096
Mind your own business.

274
00:16:07,633 --> 00:16:10,369
Ugh, why won't this move? Seriously.

275
00:16:12,071 --> 00:16:14,106
It won't move because it's stuck.

276
00:16:20,513 --> 00:16:22,081
Step aside.

277
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:35,695
Thanks.

278
00:16:40,433 --> 00:16:42,268
-Get on.
-What?

279
00:16:42,335 --> 00:16:45,071
You think you can drive with that leg?

280
00:16:45,137 --> 00:16:47,206
Hurry and get on. I'll drive.

281
00:16:50,142 --> 00:16:51,777
I said get on.

282
00:17:04,223 --> 00:17:05,892
Hold on tight.

283
00:17:11,831 --> 00:17:12,732
You'll fly off.

284
00:17:12,798 --> 00:17:14,567
Okay.

285
00:17:15,668 --> 00:17:16,802
Here we go!

286
00:17:19,005 --> 00:17:23,109
Just smiling as if perfectly happy

287
00:17:24,310 --> 00:17:26,345
Can you hear my heart?

288
00:17:26,412 --> 00:17:31,484
Should I send it on the wind?

289
00:17:32,818 --> 00:17:34,320
Come on, hold on properly.

290
00:17:34,387 --> 00:17:35,855
Forget it.

291
00:17:37,423 --> 00:17:40,626
Why? Enjoying a man's scent
for the first time in a while?

292
00:17:40,693 --> 00:17:43,362
I'm not in the mood to joke with you.

293
00:17:43,429 --> 00:17:44,797
Just drive quietly.

294
00:17:46,699 --> 00:17:48,167
Something's going on here.

295
00:17:48,234 --> 00:17:50,570
-What is it?
-Stay out of it.

296
00:17:52,538 --> 00:17:54,607
I don't see a single soul out here.

297
00:17:55,675 --> 00:17:57,076
Let's rest here a bit.

298
00:18:19,999 --> 00:18:21,867
Something's definitely going on.

299
00:18:21,934 --> 00:18:23,836
What happened?

300
00:18:24,537 --> 00:18:25,571
Talk to me.

301
00:18:26,539 --> 00:18:28,174
I told you, nothing's wrong.

302
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:30,810
Can't you drop that tough act?

303
00:18:31,677 --> 00:18:35,281
People need to know
how to lean on others sometimes.

304
00:18:35,348 --> 00:18:37,817
Making others watch you suffer alone

305
00:18:37,883 --> 00:18:40,052
isn't fair to the people around you.

306
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:44,190
That's why family and friends
are there for you to lean on.

307
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:46,425
So talk to me.

308
00:18:51,330 --> 00:18:52,565
Forget it.

309
00:18:52,632 --> 00:18:55,001
Seriously.

310
00:18:55,067 --> 00:18:58,437
If anything's too much
to handle alone, tell me.

311
00:18:59,005 --> 00:19:02,675
As a courtesy to my first love,
I'll at least hear you out.

312
00:19:02,742 --> 00:19:04,677
But you have to solve it yourself.

313
00:19:07,913 --> 00:19:10,082
Was this schoolyard always this small?

314
00:19:10,783 --> 00:19:13,019
It seemed so big back in the day.

315
00:19:13,853 --> 00:19:15,187
You're the one who grew.

316
00:19:15,254 --> 00:19:16,722
Is that it?

317
00:19:17,757 --> 00:19:19,792
Feels like we played here yesterday.

318
00:19:20,660 --> 00:19:22,261
I'm already 27.

319
00:19:22,928 --> 00:19:24,563
And you even have a kid.

320
00:19:26,298 --> 00:19:27,833
Time really flies.

321
00:19:29,402 --> 00:19:30,903
It really does.

322
00:19:33,839 --> 00:19:36,909
But will you keep living like this?

323
00:19:37,743 --> 00:19:39,779
-Won't you get married?
-Get married?

324
00:19:41,714 --> 00:19:44,316
What man would marry
a single mom like me?

325
00:19:44,383 --> 00:19:46,819
Why? What's wrong with you?

326
00:19:46,886 --> 00:19:51,190
For an unmarried woman these days
to take full responsibility for a kid,

327
00:19:51,257 --> 00:19:52,591
you think that's easy?

328
00:19:53,259 --> 00:19:55,828
That deserves an award, an award.

329
00:19:56,962 --> 00:19:58,898
To be honest with you,

330
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:02,635
I thought you were cool

331
00:20:03,302 --> 00:20:04,670
and really amazing, too.

332
00:20:05,538 --> 00:20:08,874
So don't be intimidated, and cheer up.

333
00:20:09,842 --> 00:20:12,278
You're a pretty great single mom.

334
00:20:12,344 --> 00:20:15,748
Even though your looks
took a nosedive compared to before.

335
00:20:15,815 --> 00:20:17,616
What's with you, seriously?

336
00:20:19,919 --> 00:20:23,022
See? The real you is starting to show.

337
00:20:23,089 --> 00:20:25,858
Being feisty like this suits you best.

338
00:20:25,925 --> 00:20:29,361
So I don't know what's going on,
but hang in there.

339
00:20:29,428 --> 00:20:30,496
You're middle-aged.

340
00:20:30,563 --> 00:20:31,731
Middle-aged power!

341
00:20:31,797 --> 00:20:34,066
What? Middle-aged?

342
00:20:34,934 --> 00:20:36,569
Okay, okay, okay, wait, wait!

343
00:20:37,336 --> 00:20:39,572
Wow, is this tree still here?

344
00:20:39,638 --> 00:20:42,875
I used to be this school's Spider-Man.

345
00:20:42,942 --> 00:20:44,910
Hey, you'll fall doing that!

346
00:20:44,977 --> 00:20:46,312
Oh, no, oh, no!

347
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:49,148
Unbelievable.

348
00:20:49,215 --> 00:20:50,916
Why did this tree get so big?

349
00:20:50,983 --> 00:20:53,085
Serves you right, seriously.

350
00:20:55,955 --> 00:20:57,456
Ow, my butt.

351
00:20:58,724 --> 00:21:01,794
Serves you right for goofing off.

352
00:21:01,861 --> 00:21:03,195
Come on, seriously.

353
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:06,665
That's harsh after I put on
a whole show to cheer you up.

354
00:21:06,732 --> 00:21:08,567
All right, thank you.

355
00:21:09,301 --> 00:21:12,171
You made me laugh, so I feel better.

356
00:21:12,238 --> 00:21:13,472
Forget it.

357
00:21:13,539 --> 00:21:14,907
Hurry up and get on.

358
00:21:32,591 --> 00:21:34,794
What are you doing right now?

359
00:21:34,860 --> 00:21:37,663
Know when to lean on someone, lady.

360
00:21:38,564 --> 00:21:40,232
Hold on tight.

361
00:21:42,368 --> 00:21:45,671
Shall we knock on another world?

362
00:21:45,738 --> 00:21:48,040
Knock on the door

363
00:21:48,908 --> 00:21:52,511
Will that place be translated

364
00:21:52,578 --> 00:21:55,681
Into another word for joy?

365
00:21:55,748 --> 00:22:00,152
Now let's go to the end of the sky

366
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:04,456
Min-gi, keep an eye out for thieves.

367
00:22:04,523 --> 00:22:08,327
On lookout, ma'am. Nothing in sight.

368
00:22:10,830 --> 00:22:14,466
It is finally the beginning

369
00:22:14,533 --> 00:22:17,436
Will be fine, for me

370
00:22:17,503 --> 00:22:18,938
Oh, my gosh!

371
00:22:19,004 --> 00:22:21,874
Hey! You can't stop so suddenly!

372
00:22:21,941 --> 00:22:23,709
-Yun-hui.
-What?

373
00:22:23,776 --> 00:22:25,411
That… Look at that.

374
00:22:28,347 --> 00:22:30,983
We got the ginseng. We're done.

375
00:22:31,050 --> 00:22:33,853
What is that? Are… Are they thieves?

376
00:22:33,919 --> 00:22:36,522
Hurry, go get them! Catch them!

377
00:22:36,589 --> 00:22:38,090
I'm scared.

378
00:22:38,157 --> 00:22:40,125
Should we tell the villagers first?

379
00:22:40,192 --> 00:22:42,094
What if they get away then?

380
00:22:42,161 --> 00:22:45,231
What if they have knives or something?

381
00:22:45,297 --> 00:22:47,766
You little coward, I swear…

382
00:22:47,833 --> 00:22:49,935
Hey, you filthy thieves!

383
00:22:52,671 --> 00:22:54,640
-I said hurry up and go!
-Damn it!

384
00:22:54,707 --> 00:22:56,976
-They already saw us!
-Seriously, damn it!

385
00:22:57,042 --> 00:22:58,644
Hurry, hurry, go!

386
00:22:58,711 --> 00:23:00,946
Hey! Come here! Come here, come here!

387
00:23:03,883 --> 00:23:07,319
Come here! Come here! Get over here!

388
00:23:14,460 --> 00:23:17,496
Who are you? Who are you?
Come here, come here!

389
00:23:20,666 --> 00:23:22,234
Oh, no! Min-gi!

390
00:23:29,375 --> 00:23:32,278
Min-gi, wake up!

391
00:23:32,344 --> 00:23:34,546
Min-gi, Min-gi!

392
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:37,182
Min-gi!

393
00:23:38,751 --> 00:23:40,519
SOUL HOSPITAL, REGIONAL ER CENTER

394
00:23:49,862 --> 00:23:51,563
Min-gi, are you coming to?

395
00:23:52,464 --> 00:23:54,099
Yun-hui.

396
00:23:55,567 --> 00:23:57,403
Are you okay?

397
00:23:59,138 --> 00:24:00,773
I'm okay.

398
00:24:01,974 --> 00:24:03,142
I'm fine.

399
00:24:13,252 --> 00:24:16,588
-What's wrong?
-I thought you were going to die.

400
00:24:17,856 --> 00:24:19,858
It's okay, it's okay.

401
00:24:30,135 --> 00:24:31,737
I'm fine.

402
00:24:31,804 --> 00:24:34,039
SOUL HOSPITAL

403
00:24:41,013 --> 00:24:45,484
-Seriously…
-What? Why are you laughing?

404
00:24:45,551 --> 00:24:48,220
Yun-hui, did I worry you that much?

405
00:24:48,287 --> 00:24:51,490
You cried so loud you shook
the hospital. How embarrassing.

406
00:24:51,557 --> 00:24:53,692
I didn't cry out of worry for you.

407
00:24:53,759 --> 00:24:56,895
I cried over wasting money
on the hospital bill. So what?

408
00:24:56,962 --> 00:24:58,564
You're such a liar.

409
00:24:58,630 --> 00:25:00,933
I should've gotten that on video.

410
00:25:03,135 --> 00:25:04,770
Why, you little…

411
00:25:10,542 --> 00:25:12,511
Are you in pain? Are you okay?

412
00:25:13,345 --> 00:25:15,848
I'm hungry. Buy me food.

413
00:25:15,914 --> 00:25:18,183
What? You little punk!

414
00:25:18,250 --> 00:25:19,985
If you don't buy me food,

415
00:25:20,052 --> 00:25:21,687
I'll tell the whole village

416
00:25:21,754 --> 00:25:23,489
that you bawled like a baby.

417
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:26,592
What do you want to eat?

418
00:25:28,894 --> 00:25:30,062
Spaghetti.

419
00:25:35,100 --> 00:25:36,568
You call this spaghetti?

420
00:25:37,536 --> 00:25:39,705
I said I wanted spaghetti. Spaghetti!

421
00:25:39,772 --> 00:25:42,041
There's no spaghetti in the country.

422
00:25:42,107 --> 00:25:43,542
Unbelievable.

423
00:25:43,609 --> 00:25:45,444
-Then don't eat it.
-Darn it.

424
00:25:45,511 --> 00:25:46,678
Who said I wouldn't?

425
00:25:49,648 --> 00:25:52,885
Anyway, since I bought you this,

426
00:25:53,552 --> 00:25:55,254
keep my crying today a secret.

427
00:25:55,320 --> 00:25:56,889
Depends on how you treat me.

428
00:25:56,955 --> 00:25:58,757
You little brat, I swear…

429
00:26:00,959 --> 00:26:01,860
Where to?

430
00:26:01,927 --> 00:26:03,629
To the bathroom. Why?

431
00:26:06,331 --> 00:26:07,900
Seriously.

432
00:26:07,966 --> 00:26:11,003
Why did tears fall right then,
of all times? Why tears?

433
00:26:13,939 --> 00:26:17,309
I was harboring an ingrate in my home.

434
00:26:17,376 --> 00:26:19,778
How dare a freeloader like you… What?

435
00:26:20,345 --> 00:26:22,481
You stole and ate our sweet potatoes?

436
00:26:22,548 --> 00:26:24,583
Um, sir, I didn't steal them.

437
00:26:24,650 --> 00:26:25,951
-Just a prank--
-Shut up!

438
00:26:26,018 --> 00:26:27,486
A prank, my foot!

439
00:26:27,553 --> 00:26:30,489
With the town in turmoil over a thief,

440
00:26:30,556 --> 00:26:32,925
are you out of your mind or what?

441
00:26:32,991 --> 00:26:35,794
Your friend cracked his skull
catching the thief

442
00:26:35,861 --> 00:26:37,863
and landed in the hospital, got it?

443
00:26:40,532 --> 00:26:41,700
-Hey!
-Bro, you okay?

444
00:26:41,767 --> 00:26:44,369
I just got a few stitches. I'm fine.

445
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:47,639
What a relief. Thank goodness.

446
00:26:49,675 --> 00:26:50,909
Um…

447
00:26:50,976 --> 00:26:54,146
I'm sorry to ask when you just
came from the hospital.

448
00:26:55,314 --> 00:26:56,982
But do you remember anything?

449
00:26:57,049 --> 00:26:58,650
Like the license plate?

450
00:26:59,418 --> 00:27:02,488
They completely covered
the license plate with tape.

451
00:27:02,554 --> 00:27:04,156
They covered it?

452
00:27:04,857 --> 00:27:06,792
Uh, then what about the face?

453
00:27:08,927 --> 00:27:11,897
I don't remember the exact details.

454
00:27:14,366 --> 00:27:17,536
But there's one thing I do remember.

455
00:27:17,603 --> 00:27:20,105
Really? What is it?

456
00:27:21,006 --> 00:27:22,174
The eyes.

457
00:27:22,741 --> 00:27:26,178
Their eyes were really pretty.

458
00:27:26,245 --> 00:27:29,381
They had deep double eyelids
and plump lower eyelids.

459
00:27:31,683 --> 00:27:33,886
Their eyes were pretty?

460
00:27:34,686 --> 00:27:36,388
Then what about the face?

461
00:27:38,490 --> 00:27:41,760
The face is hazy to me.
I can almost remember it, though.

462
00:27:42,728 --> 00:27:46,098
In that case, you know,
should we draw a composite sketch?

463
00:27:46,165 --> 00:27:50,135
You see them draw composite sketches
to catch criminals in the movies.

464
00:27:50,202 --> 00:27:53,372
A composite sketch?
But who would draw that?

465
00:27:54,139 --> 00:27:58,644
Oh! There's that young woman
who paints murals in our village.

466
00:27:58,710 --> 00:28:00,445
That's right.

467
00:28:06,218 --> 00:28:09,087
Their eyes were very pretty.

468
00:28:18,830 --> 00:28:22,868
And they had very deep double eyelids.

469
00:28:23,468 --> 00:28:24,870
And their nose

470
00:28:26,371 --> 00:28:28,340
was high and well-defined.

471
00:28:32,611 --> 00:28:35,080
Wait, no, no, that's not it.

472
00:28:35,147 --> 00:28:37,816
The lips were a bit thinner than this.

473
00:28:41,587 --> 00:28:43,422
That's it, that's it.

474
00:28:43,488 --> 00:28:45,624
They looked like this. Yes, so close.

475
00:28:45,691 --> 00:28:46,558
-Really?
-Yes.

476
00:28:46,625 --> 00:28:47,859
Let me see.

477
00:28:53,899 --> 00:28:57,269
Is this a thief
or the lead in a romance comic?

478
00:29:00,572 --> 00:29:01,740
Really? Like this?

479
00:29:01,807 --> 00:29:04,276
Uh, kind of, and kind of not.

480
00:29:04,343 --> 00:29:06,278
But the eyes are spot-on. The eyes.

481
00:29:06,345 --> 00:29:07,579
Forget it, forget it!

482
00:29:07,646 --> 00:29:10,048
How can we catch the thief with this?

483
00:29:10,115 --> 00:29:12,551
Why, those rotten jerks! Just wait!

484
00:29:12,618 --> 00:29:15,454
Gosh, anyway, what do we do now?

485
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:17,489
Well, there's nothing we can do.

486
00:29:17,556 --> 00:29:20,959
All we can do is install CCTV
and step up our patrols.

487
00:29:21,026 --> 00:29:22,894
Let's head to the cabbage field now.

488
00:29:22,961 --> 00:29:24,229
Sure, let's go.

489
00:29:24,296 --> 00:29:26,231
Hey! You, halt right where you are!

490
00:29:26,798 --> 00:29:28,900
Ow, sir! What are you doing?

491
00:29:28,967 --> 00:29:30,302
You thieving bastard!

492
00:29:30,369 --> 00:29:32,971
You stole my sweet potatoes.
Where are you going?

493
00:29:33,038 --> 00:29:34,973
You're my slave all day. My slave!

494
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:37,676
Work off the sweet potatoes
you dug up. Got it?

495
00:29:37,743 --> 00:29:39,044
Get up, get up, get up.

496
00:29:39,111 --> 00:29:40,946
Get up, come on. Get outside.

497
00:29:41,013 --> 00:29:42,614
Get out there, you punk.

498
00:29:45,083 --> 00:29:47,052
-Get out, get out!
-Ow, sir!

499
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:52,658
Those rotten jerks.

500
00:29:53,358 --> 00:29:54,793
Just let me catch them.

501
00:29:54,860 --> 00:29:56,094
They look so tasty!

502
00:29:57,729 --> 00:29:59,498
What are you doing right now?

503
00:30:00,198 --> 00:30:01,667
I asked what you're doing!

504
00:30:04,136 --> 00:30:05,404
Um, well…

505
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:08,006
we only picked a few to taste.

506
00:30:08,073 --> 00:30:09,541
I don't care if it's a few!

507
00:30:09,608 --> 00:30:12,177
Who said you could pick
from someone else's field?

508
00:30:12,244 --> 00:30:14,680
You're being way too harsh, mister.

509
00:30:14,746 --> 00:30:16,348
It's not even a big deal.

510
00:30:16,415 --> 00:30:17,783
What, not a big deal?

511
00:30:17,849 --> 00:30:20,018
How dare you say that! How dare you!

512
00:30:20,085 --> 00:30:22,921
Hey, man! Why are you doing this?
Calm down!

513
00:30:22,988 --> 00:30:25,257
Calm down, my foot! They're thieves!

514
00:30:25,324 --> 00:30:26,658
Sang-deuk, get the cops!

515
00:30:26,725 --> 00:30:30,329
Thieves? We only picked a few apples!

516
00:30:30,395 --> 00:30:32,931
Gosh, so much for country generosity.

517
00:30:32,998 --> 00:30:34,132
Generosity?

518
00:30:34,199 --> 00:30:36,735
Is country generosity
when they strip my field

519
00:30:36,802 --> 00:30:38,503
and I just let it go?

520
00:30:38,570 --> 00:30:42,207
We broke our backs for months
to grow these, you know that?

521
00:30:42,274 --> 00:30:43,809
Stop it, man.

522
00:30:45,010 --> 00:30:46,311
Um, please understand.

523
00:30:46,378 --> 00:30:48,213
Thieves are rampant here lately.

524
00:30:49,181 --> 00:30:50,515
Ladies, as you pass by,

525
00:30:50,582 --> 00:30:52,384
you may pick a few just for fun.

526
00:30:52,451 --> 00:30:54,119
But if one by one people do it,

527
00:30:54,186 --> 00:30:55,921
the damage to farmers is huge.

528
00:30:56,588 --> 00:30:58,223
Take what you picked to eat.

529
00:30:58,290 --> 00:31:00,959
Next time, please understand
our situation, okay?

530
00:31:02,427 --> 00:31:05,263
-We're so sorry.
-I'm sorry.

531
00:31:11,169 --> 00:31:12,938
Man-gu's in a stormy mood.

532
00:31:13,004 --> 00:31:14,172
I know.

533
00:31:14,239 --> 00:31:16,341
We can't ask for cabbage tips for now.

534
00:31:16,408 --> 00:31:18,410
Do you think he's in the mood now?

535
00:31:18,477 --> 00:31:21,079
I'll help you out today, so let's go.

536
00:31:22,214 --> 00:31:23,949
Though Man-gu yells and nags,

537
00:31:24,015 --> 00:31:25,350
he taught you well.

538
00:31:25,417 --> 00:31:27,652
-You planted them well!
-We did, right?

539
00:31:40,799 --> 00:31:43,001
-Hey.
-What?

540
00:31:43,068 --> 00:31:44,770
Where did all the seedlings go?

541
00:31:44,836 --> 00:31:45,837
What do you mean?

542
00:31:46,571 --> 00:31:50,108
-Do people steal seedlings too?
-Might as well rob a beggar!

543
00:31:50,175 --> 00:31:52,778
Of all things to steal,
you even steal seedlings?

544
00:31:54,112 --> 00:31:55,781
I don't think thieves did this.

545
00:31:55,847 --> 00:31:58,150
-Then who was it?
-Water deer.

546
00:31:58,216 --> 00:32:01,386
-Water deer?
-Their footprints are all over here.

547
00:32:01,453 --> 00:32:04,723
They just love these cabbage sprouts.

548
00:32:07,893 --> 00:32:11,096
It's one thing after another.
Water deer and even thieves.

549
00:32:11,163 --> 00:32:14,099
Water deer are far more terrifying
than thieves.

550
00:32:14,166 --> 00:32:16,768
Do they understand us?
Do they fear the police?

551
00:32:16,835 --> 00:32:19,204
-So what should we do?
-You just stand guard.

552
00:32:19,271 --> 00:32:21,506
Some people hook up loudspeakers

553
00:32:21,573 --> 00:32:23,341
to play a radio all night, I hear.

554
00:32:24,009 --> 00:32:26,711
Deer think someone's here
and stay away, supposedly.

555
00:32:26,778 --> 00:32:30,849
But man, this place is way too huge.

556
00:32:30,916 --> 00:32:33,251
So what are we supposed to do now?

557
00:32:33,318 --> 00:32:36,521
-Hey, how about we do this?
-Do what?

558
00:33:06,418 --> 00:33:07,886
Hey, wait, wait, wait!

559
00:33:07,953 --> 00:33:10,522
Do we really have to keep doing this?

560
00:33:10,589 --> 00:33:13,058
Does this even work at all?

561
00:33:13,124 --> 00:33:14,726
It's better than nothing.

562
00:33:14,793 --> 00:33:17,362
Plus, it's good practice too.

563
00:33:17,429 --> 00:33:19,965
Still, playing together again is fun.

564
00:33:20,532 --> 00:33:22,100
Fun, my ass. Seriously.

565
00:33:29,875 --> 00:33:33,111
Move it faster, you slave!

566
00:33:33,178 --> 00:33:34,246
Ow, that stings!

567
00:33:34,312 --> 00:33:36,181
Sir, aren't you going too far?

568
00:33:36,848 --> 00:33:38,049
What?

569
00:33:38,116 --> 00:33:40,785
This is nothing
compared to what you did.

570
00:33:40,852 --> 00:33:43,889
In the old days,
you'd be drawn and quartered!

571
00:33:44,556 --> 00:33:45,991
Yes, sir.

572
00:33:46,057 --> 00:33:48,426
Hey, set it down now.

573
00:33:50,095 --> 00:33:52,797
I'll go grab a glass of makgeolli,

574
00:33:52,864 --> 00:33:54,966
so you pack these into boxes

575
00:33:55,033 --> 00:33:57,369
and stack them neatly
in the shed, got it?

576
00:33:57,435 --> 00:33:59,104
All right, keep at it.

577
00:34:02,040 --> 00:34:03,308
Seriously.

578
00:34:04,910 --> 00:34:07,379
I'm so tired it's killing me.

579
00:34:11,917 --> 00:34:13,618
Su-yeon!

580
00:34:15,153 --> 00:34:17,155
Han-cheol.

581
00:34:17,222 --> 00:34:18,123
Hello.

582
00:34:18,189 --> 00:34:19,891
I'm sorry. It's because of me.

583
00:34:19,958 --> 00:34:21,993
It's fine, really.

584
00:34:22,060 --> 00:34:23,995
I'm just glad you didn't get caught.

585
00:34:24,663 --> 00:34:25,564
Thank you.

586
00:34:25,630 --> 00:34:27,766
Then could you do me one favor?

587
00:34:28,500 --> 00:34:30,201
A favor?

588
00:34:30,268 --> 00:34:31,136
What is it?

589
00:34:32,971 --> 00:34:34,573
Please go on one date with me.

590
00:34:34,639 --> 00:34:35,507
Excuse me?

591
00:34:39,477 --> 00:34:40,545
Put these away.

592
00:34:58,430 --> 00:35:01,499
Know when to lean on someone, lady.

593
00:35:04,970 --> 00:35:07,672
What am I even thinking right now?

594
00:35:08,340 --> 00:35:10,942
I'm crazy, I'm seriously crazy.

595
00:35:11,610 --> 00:35:13,545
-What are you doing?
-You scared me!

596
00:35:15,347 --> 00:35:16,214
Why so jumpy?

597
00:35:16,281 --> 00:35:18,516
Because you barged right in, you jerk.

598
00:35:18,583 --> 00:35:21,386
Why are you snapping at me again?
What did I do?

599
00:35:23,622 --> 00:35:24,923
Make us some coffee.

600
00:35:24,990 --> 00:35:27,459
Coffee? Why coffee?

601
00:35:27,525 --> 00:35:30,028
That water deer ate all our seedlings.

602
00:35:30,095 --> 00:35:31,796
We have to guard them all night.

603
00:35:31,863 --> 00:35:33,298
Make me some coffee.

604
00:35:33,365 --> 00:35:37,535
Coffee? Don't you have hands and feet?
Why should I do it?

605
00:35:37,602 --> 00:35:41,106
Oh, so you won't be making it, then?

606
00:35:42,974 --> 00:35:44,142
You'll regret this.

607
00:35:44,209 --> 00:35:45,610
Regret?

608
00:35:46,478 --> 00:35:47,946
I'll have you know,

609
00:35:48,013 --> 00:35:51,149
I've never had a regret in my life.

610
00:35:51,216 --> 00:35:52,851
Is that so?

611
00:35:52,917 --> 00:35:54,686
Hey, should I tell a funny story?

612
00:35:54,753 --> 00:35:56,688
-Earlier, the hospital--
-Okay, fine!

613
00:35:56,755 --> 00:35:59,024
I'll make it for you right now.

614
00:35:59,090 --> 00:36:01,893
Jeez, he's my worst enemy, I swear.

615
00:36:04,262 --> 00:36:07,098
Anyway, that woman is so ignorant.

616
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:10,535
Hey, is this coffee or what?
Is it mountain spring water?

617
00:36:10,602 --> 00:36:12,604
She could've at least made Americano.

618
00:36:12,671 --> 00:36:14,472
Who drinks sweet instant coffee…

619
00:36:26,251 --> 00:36:27,585
Hello.

620
00:36:35,060 --> 00:36:36,394
Is she gone?

621
00:36:36,461 --> 00:36:39,531
What are you doing?
Is this because you saw your wife?

622
00:36:43,001 --> 00:36:44,469
I hate seeing that woman.

623
00:36:44,536 --> 00:36:46,438
Things get weird and I get blamed.

624
00:36:46,504 --> 00:36:48,473
-You hate her that much?
-I hate her.

625
00:36:49,040 --> 00:36:50,742
I really hate her! Jeez.

626
00:37:45,363 --> 00:37:47,599
The weather keeps getting colder.

627
00:37:49,434 --> 00:37:50,902
Sir, what are you doing?

628
00:37:54,639 --> 00:37:57,175
-Is he a kleptomaniac?
-Why touch my guitar?

629
00:38:03,681 --> 00:38:05,984
-Hey, hurry!
-Come on, seriously!

630
00:38:06,951 --> 00:38:09,654
Jeez, those punks are losing it fast.

631
00:38:10,722 --> 00:38:13,091
-Open it, hurry!
-Hey, hurry, wait a sec!

632
00:38:24,202 --> 00:38:27,405
I'm exhausted at the crack of dawn.

633
00:38:27,472 --> 00:38:28,873
That deer kept me awake.

634
00:38:28,940 --> 00:38:31,843
Seriously, why am I getting annoyed?

635
00:38:31,910 --> 00:38:34,112
Today's a day to be totally pumped up!

636
00:38:34,879 --> 00:38:37,382
Sorry, guys.

637
00:38:37,448 --> 00:38:40,451
I'll work double when I get back.

638
00:38:40,518 --> 00:38:44,055
Though I might not come back tonight.

639
00:38:44,122 --> 00:38:44,989
SOUL STATION

640
00:38:45,056 --> 00:38:48,126
I have no time to dig the ground.
Who needs a date? Jeez.

641
00:38:48,960 --> 00:38:52,564
Still, he even took the blame for me,
so I couldn't just not come.

642
00:38:52,630 --> 00:38:54,566
I'm losing my mind, seriously.

643
00:38:56,734 --> 00:38:58,069
Since it's come to this,

644
00:38:58,136 --> 00:39:00,738
I'll make him get over me for good.

645
00:39:02,373 --> 00:39:04,008
Su-yeon!

646
00:39:07,412 --> 00:39:09,981
I'll officially confess to her today.

647
00:39:10,048 --> 00:39:12,150
You've got this, Han-cheol!

648
00:39:13,451 --> 00:39:17,355
It's cold, isn't it?
We only get summer and winter now.

649
00:39:18,022 --> 00:39:21,826
I planned a fantastic date for today.

650
00:39:21,893 --> 00:39:22,961
Look forward to it.

651
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:24,762
Okay.

652
00:39:24,829 --> 00:39:25,964
Shall we go?

653
00:39:32,003 --> 00:39:33,838
I swear.

654
00:39:33,905 --> 00:39:36,007
My butt is killing me, seriously.

655
00:39:36,074 --> 00:39:38,142
Is this how you treat a patient?

656
00:39:38,209 --> 00:39:40,445
This is actually the prime spot.

657
00:39:40,511 --> 00:39:43,214
Prime spot? Like hell.
My butt's about to break.

658
00:39:44,949 --> 00:39:48,186
Quit grumbling and look at the sky.

659
00:39:48,253 --> 00:39:49,888
Why the sky now?

660
00:39:56,094 --> 00:39:59,330
I think the sky's prettiest from here.

661
00:40:00,131 --> 00:40:02,734
-How is it?
-Was the sky always this blue?

662
00:40:03,835 --> 00:40:05,770
I've never seen a sky this pretty.

663
00:40:06,537 --> 00:40:07,872
Actually, no.

664
00:40:08,907 --> 00:40:11,209
I barely remember
when I last saw the sky.

665
00:40:11,276 --> 00:40:14,045
Look all you want.

666
00:40:14,112 --> 00:40:17,115
Min-gi, spread your arms.
Do this and we'll fly.

667
00:40:17,181 --> 00:40:18,449
Come on, hurry!

668
00:40:18,516 --> 00:40:19,851
-Like this?
-Right.

669
00:40:19,918 --> 00:40:22,487
Move your arms like this. Faster!

670
00:40:22,553 --> 00:40:23,454
Faster, faster!

671
00:40:23,521 --> 00:40:25,924
What am I even doing right now?

672
00:40:29,193 --> 00:40:30,962
My butt is killing me.

673
00:40:31,629 --> 00:40:33,798
A grown man making such a fuss.

674
00:40:33,865 --> 00:40:36,234
Anyway, what's all that racket?

675
00:40:36,301 --> 00:40:37,702
Is it a medicine peddler?

676
00:40:39,904 --> 00:40:43,074
EDIYA COFFEE HADUROK-RI BRANCH

677
00:40:43,841 --> 00:40:46,377
Our coffee shop just opened.
Please come often!

678
00:40:46,444 --> 00:40:49,314
-Isn't that Mi-yeong?
-Yes, have a nice day!

679
00:40:49,380 --> 00:40:52,583
We just opened our coffee shop!
Please stop by often!

680
00:40:52,650 --> 00:40:54,585
You're right, it's Mi-yeong.

681
00:40:55,553 --> 00:40:56,955
Mi-yeong!

682
00:40:58,723 --> 00:41:00,325
Yun-hui!

683
00:41:00,959 --> 00:41:02,927
Yun-hui!

684
00:41:02,994 --> 00:41:05,596
What brings you here? It's been ages!

685
00:41:05,663 --> 00:41:09,167
I know. I'm on my way to the hospital.

686
00:41:09,233 --> 00:41:11,102
But what is all this?

687
00:41:11,169 --> 00:41:14,172
It's our coffee shop's grand opening.

688
00:41:14,238 --> 00:41:18,710
A grand opening?
You should've told me in advance.

689
00:41:18,776 --> 00:41:20,912
Everyone's busy, so why make a fuss?

690
00:41:20,979 --> 00:41:23,081
Since you're here, come in for coffee.

691
00:41:23,147 --> 00:41:24,882
Um… I'm busy, so I should go.

692
00:41:24,949 --> 00:41:28,052
Hey, punk, you just came out
for athlete's foot medicine!

693
00:41:28,119 --> 00:41:31,222
Busy, my foot. Let's grab a cup, bud.

694
00:41:34,993 --> 00:41:36,961
A place like this opened in town?

695
00:41:38,363 --> 00:41:40,565
This place looks pretty fancy.

696
00:41:40,631 --> 00:41:43,234
Even our township got a coffee shop.

697
00:41:43,301 --> 00:41:47,138
An iced Americano!
Hey, how long has it been?

698
00:41:49,907 --> 00:41:51,442
It's so good.

699
00:41:54,045 --> 00:41:55,179
Gosh, it's bitter!

700
00:41:55,246 --> 00:41:58,016
Hey, got any sugar? And creamer?

701
00:41:58,082 --> 00:41:59,450
So uncultured, seriously.

702
00:41:59,517 --> 00:42:02,220
Just drink it. You drink it like this.

703
00:42:03,388 --> 00:42:06,090
Must be nice knowing so much, you brat.

704
00:42:06,157 --> 00:42:09,427
Wait, you're the owner,
and you even serve tables yourself?

705
00:42:09,494 --> 00:42:11,896
I actually put up a part-timer sign.

706
00:42:11,963 --> 00:42:14,699
Only grandmas and grandpas keep asking.

707
00:42:14,766 --> 00:42:17,802
Gosh, I need to hire someone.
This is a real problem.

708
00:42:17,869 --> 00:42:20,238
Hey, should I do it?

709
00:42:20,304 --> 00:42:21,572
You?

710
00:42:21,639 --> 00:42:23,241
My dream is to be a barista.

711
00:42:24,642 --> 00:42:27,845
Oh, don't make me laugh,
gag, and choke on that nonsense!

712
00:42:27,912 --> 00:42:30,048
Until recently, it was a nail artist.

713
00:42:30,114 --> 00:42:32,183
And before that, some tattoo artist.

714
00:42:32,250 --> 00:42:33,851
I'm serious this time, okay?

715
00:42:33,918 --> 00:42:36,654
Beans from Colombia, Kenya,
Costa Rica, Guatemala…

716
00:42:36,721 --> 00:42:39,023
Okay, okay. Do whatever you want.

717
00:42:40,258 --> 00:42:42,126
Hey, I'll do it. I will!

718
00:42:42,193 --> 00:42:45,163
Then that's great for me.
I'll have someone to talk to.

719
00:42:45,229 --> 00:42:47,198
Okay, when should I start?

720
00:42:47,265 --> 00:42:48,900
No, I'll just start today.

721
00:42:48,966 --> 00:42:51,102
Should I start by handing out flyers?

722
00:42:51,736 --> 00:42:54,038
Gosh, that little brat, I swear…

723
00:42:54,105 --> 00:42:57,341
Right, I heard we had a thief in town.

724
00:42:57,408 --> 00:43:00,411
Yes, Man-gu's ginseng field
was completely cleaned out.

725
00:43:00,478 --> 00:43:02,380
Min-gi busted his head. It's chaos.

726
00:43:02,447 --> 00:43:03,981
If I catch those bastards,

727
00:43:04,048 --> 00:43:07,185
I'll snap their legs right in half!

728
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:09,487
Gosh, bringing it up again burns me up.

729
00:43:14,625 --> 00:43:16,294
Thank you.

730
00:43:17,361 --> 00:43:19,097
Um, Su-yeon.

731
00:43:19,664 --> 00:43:22,100
I checked, and they say this train here

732
00:43:22,166 --> 00:43:24,435
is the best for dates, the very best!

733
00:43:24,502 --> 00:43:25,837
Is that so?

734
00:43:25,903 --> 00:43:27,405
Um… Excuse me, Su-yeon.

735
00:43:27,472 --> 00:43:28,339
Just a moment.

736
00:43:28,406 --> 00:43:32,343
Um, I have one humble favor to ask.

737
00:43:32,410 --> 00:43:33,878
What is it?

738
00:43:37,915 --> 00:43:39,283
Ta-da!

739
00:43:41,452 --> 00:43:43,154
It's a matching couple shirt.

740
00:43:43,221 --> 00:43:45,556
Could you wear it just once?
It's my wish.

741
00:43:50,561 --> 00:43:52,463
You don't have to if you hate it.

742
00:43:52,530 --> 00:43:55,600
Even I think it's childish and tacky.

743
00:43:57,068 --> 00:43:58,536
All right, fine.

744
00:43:58,603 --> 00:44:00,471
I'll wear it. Give it to me.

745
00:44:03,708 --> 00:44:04,876
Thank you!

746
00:44:04,942 --> 00:44:07,078
Isn't it cute? It looks like you.

747
00:44:07,145 --> 00:44:09,046
I think you look like a dog.

748
00:44:09,881 --> 00:44:10,882
A dog.

749
00:44:10,948 --> 00:44:13,384
Since I feel bad,
I'll even wear this, jeez.

750
00:44:13,451 --> 00:44:16,420
If I find a good chance
to reason with him, he'll get it.

751
00:44:21,526 --> 00:44:24,929
Wow, this train is so pretty, really.

752
00:44:25,696 --> 00:44:26,864
Wow, this is so nice.

753
00:44:26,931 --> 00:44:29,033
Su-yeon, have a seat, have a seat.

754
00:44:32,069 --> 00:44:33,604
Gosh, it's really great.

755
00:44:34,672 --> 00:44:38,476
Oh! What's this? The window opens too!

756
00:44:38,543 --> 00:44:40,778
-So it does.
-This is so cool.

757
00:44:40,845 --> 00:44:42,046
Wow, it's great.

758
00:44:42,113 --> 00:44:44,115
Su-yeon, aren't you hungry?

759
00:44:44,182 --> 00:44:46,184
I prepared something for you…

760
00:44:46,884 --> 00:44:48,052
What is it this time?

761
00:44:51,756 --> 00:44:53,891
Ta-da! Sweet potatoes, your favorite!

762
00:44:56,394 --> 00:44:57,828
And…

763
00:44:59,063 --> 00:45:02,166
a perfect match for sweet potatoes,
15-year-aged kimchi!

764
00:45:05,336 --> 00:45:07,438
Now, here's how we eat this.

765
00:45:08,206 --> 00:45:09,440
But I'm not hungry…

766
00:45:09,507 --> 00:45:11,142
Come on, I'll do it for you.

767
00:45:11,209 --> 00:45:13,678
Snap a sweet potato in half like this.

768
00:45:13,744 --> 00:45:15,613
Mmm, boy, and right here,

769
00:45:15,680 --> 00:45:19,650
slap on a piece or two of kimchi,
and slap it right on top like this.

770
00:45:21,285 --> 00:45:22,520
No, no thanks.

771
00:45:22,587 --> 00:45:24,488
-Try some. Say ah.
-No thanks.

772
00:45:24,555 --> 00:45:25,823
Come on, hurry.

773
00:45:25,890 --> 00:45:27,325
-Let me do it.
-One bite.

774
00:45:27,391 --> 00:45:29,126
Let me do it!

775
00:45:36,000 --> 00:45:38,202
I am so sorry. I am so sorry.

776
00:45:38,936 --> 00:45:40,671
Sorry, my foot.

777
00:45:42,139 --> 00:45:45,042
I need to dump this guy right away.

778
00:45:51,082 --> 00:45:52,917
I'm so sorry. What can I do?

779
00:45:52,984 --> 00:45:55,653
-Let me see, I'll--
-Stop, I said forget it.

780
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:58,055
-Watch your hands.
-I am sorry.

781
00:45:58,122 --> 00:45:59,890
I made a mistake…

782
00:46:03,894 --> 00:46:07,231
Um, Han-cheol, I have something to say.

783
00:46:08,099 --> 00:46:09,567
Please go ahead, go ahead.

784
00:46:13,437 --> 00:46:15,606
Han-cheol, you're a really good person.

785
00:46:17,975 --> 00:46:19,977
I know that too.

786
00:46:22,580 --> 00:46:26,017
And I know you're too good for me.

787
00:46:26,083 --> 00:46:28,953
Well, uh, you're too kind.

788
00:46:29,020 --> 00:46:31,455
You're making me blush, really.

789
00:46:35,760 --> 00:46:38,029
But Han-cheol, I…

790
00:46:38,095 --> 00:46:39,297
Su-yeon, look out!

791
00:46:47,104 --> 00:46:48,372
Oh my, Han-cheol!

792
00:46:48,439 --> 00:46:50,207
Han-cheol! Han-cheol!

793
00:46:50,841 --> 00:46:52,076
Are you okay?

794
00:46:52,143 --> 00:46:56,981
BUNCHEON STATION

795
00:46:57,048 --> 00:46:58,783
Are you okay, Han-cheol?

796
00:46:58,849 --> 00:47:00,284
I'm fine, Su-yeon.

797
00:47:00,351 --> 00:47:02,153
Why would that suddenly fall?

798
00:47:03,020 --> 00:47:05,456
Without him, you'd be badly hurt, miss.

799
00:47:07,124 --> 00:47:09,994
Uh, right. Thank you for your help.

800
00:47:10,061 --> 00:47:13,030
-Yes, I'm sorry about that.
-Thank you.

801
00:47:14,231 --> 00:47:16,267
Thank you, Han-cheol.

802
00:47:16,334 --> 00:47:19,170
Gosh, I said it was nothing, Su-yeon.

803
00:47:19,236 --> 00:47:22,773
I'm just so relieved you weren't hurt.

804
00:47:22,840 --> 00:47:26,177
So what were you about to say earlier?

805
00:47:26,243 --> 00:47:27,578
Sorry?

806
00:47:27,645 --> 00:47:31,582
Um, well, it's just…

807
00:47:33,551 --> 00:47:36,187
What is it? Feel free to tell me.

808
00:47:37,221 --> 00:47:39,590
Um, well…

809
00:47:41,425 --> 00:47:43,194
I mean…

810
00:47:45,229 --> 00:47:46,797
About your feelings, I…

811
00:47:56,907 --> 00:47:58,175
Blood.

812
00:47:59,243 --> 00:48:00,378
I'm totally fine.

813
00:48:00,444 --> 00:48:02,980
My head's cracked,
so of course it's bleeding.

814
00:48:03,047 --> 00:48:04,215
It's normal. So normal.

815
00:48:04,281 --> 00:48:05,149
Please go on.

816
00:48:05,216 --> 00:48:07,918
It's just, um…

817
00:48:11,922 --> 00:48:13,257
It was nothing.

818
00:48:14,158 --> 00:48:15,493
Is that right?

819
00:48:15,559 --> 00:48:18,095
Then let's head to our next stop.

820
00:48:19,997 --> 00:48:22,633
-Goodbye, come again.
-Goodbye.

821
00:48:24,201 --> 00:48:27,271
There's quite a crowd for opening day.

822
00:48:27,338 --> 00:48:29,774
Right? You'll get rich, Mi-yeong.

823
00:48:29,840 --> 00:48:33,110
Come on, it's just for the experience.

824
00:48:33,177 --> 00:48:34,879
I'm not in it for the money.

825
00:48:34,945 --> 00:48:37,581
I heard you married into a rich family.

826
00:48:37,648 --> 00:48:39,583
You must've gotten hefty alimony.

827
00:48:40,351 --> 00:48:42,920
Man-gu, what are you saying right now?

828
00:48:42,987 --> 00:48:45,022
It was a joke. I'm sorry.

829
00:48:45,089 --> 00:48:47,124
-Just a joke.
-That's all right.

830
00:48:47,191 --> 00:48:48,959
Hey, Man-su, this place looks new.

831
00:48:49,026 --> 00:48:50,928
Customers! I'll take their order.

832
00:48:50,995 --> 00:48:52,630
Welcome!

833
00:48:52,696 --> 00:48:54,832
Here is the coffee you ordered.

834
00:48:54,899 --> 00:48:56,634
Please enjoy.

835
00:48:56,700 --> 00:48:57,568
What's this?

836
00:48:59,503 --> 00:49:01,071
You're just leaving?

837
00:49:01,138 --> 00:49:02,740
Excuse me?

838
00:49:02,807 --> 00:49:04,809
Come sit with us before you go.

839
00:49:06,110 --> 00:49:08,846
Sir, this isn't a tea parlor.

840
00:49:08,913 --> 00:49:10,281
I apologize.

841
00:49:12,883 --> 00:49:15,653
Such a pretty lady, being so fussy.

842
00:49:15,719 --> 00:49:17,755
Sit down, sit down.

843
00:49:17,822 --> 00:49:21,492
-Sit down.
-What are you doing? Let go of me!

844
00:49:22,226 --> 00:49:24,061
How about you let go of her?

845
00:49:25,062 --> 00:49:26,063
And what's this?

846
00:49:26,697 --> 00:49:28,466
A neighborhood friend. Why?

847
00:49:29,166 --> 00:49:31,302
Let go while I'm still asking nicely.

848
00:49:35,473 --> 00:49:37,708
What will you do if I don't let go?

849
00:49:38,576 --> 00:49:39,944
Why, you little punk…

850
00:49:40,010 --> 00:49:42,012
Do you need to learn the hard way?

851
00:49:45,049 --> 00:49:47,051
-My finger!
-Hey!

852
00:49:47,117 --> 00:49:49,920
Sang-deuk! Hey, let go of his hand!

853
00:49:49,987 --> 00:49:52,389
Let go right now, you bastard!

854
00:49:54,325 --> 00:49:56,760
What, "bastard"? Are you crazy, lady?

855
00:49:56,827 --> 00:50:00,397
Hey! What are you guys? Are you thugs?

856
00:50:02,433 --> 00:50:03,601
Go or I call the cops!

857
00:50:03,667 --> 00:50:06,270
-Huh?
-What? The cops?

858
00:50:07,571 --> 00:50:08,772
Go on, call them.

859
00:50:08,839 --> 00:50:10,674
Call them, you little bitch.

860
00:50:10,741 --> 00:50:12,376
I should just smack you!

861
00:50:12,943 --> 00:50:15,179
Are you going to hit me right now?

862
00:50:15,679 --> 00:50:16,547
Please, hit me.

863
00:50:16,614 --> 00:50:18,916
Please, hit me! I said hit me! Hit me!

864
00:50:18,983 --> 00:50:20,484
Hit me, you punk! Hit me!

865
00:50:20,551 --> 00:50:22,987
Is this bitch crazy? Damn it!

866
00:50:23,754 --> 00:50:26,123
-Yun-hui, are you okay?
-Ow, Min-gi.

867
00:50:26,190 --> 00:50:27,858
You bastard!

868
00:50:28,726 --> 00:50:29,727
What? You punk!

869
00:51:31,422 --> 00:51:32,823
Hey! Let's go.

870
00:51:32,890 --> 00:51:34,792
That was seriously disgusting.

871
00:51:34,858 --> 00:51:36,093
Wait!

872
00:51:45,936 --> 00:51:47,004
What are you doing?

873
00:51:47,071 --> 00:51:48,639
-It was you, right?
-What?

874
00:51:48,706 --> 00:51:51,942
You're that ginseng field thief!

875
00:51:56,547 --> 00:51:59,149
I don't know what you're talking about.

876
00:51:59,216 --> 00:52:01,118
Those eyes!

877
00:52:02,019 --> 00:52:03,721
I remember your eyes.

878
00:52:03,787 --> 00:52:06,256
Right? You're that thief, right?

879
00:52:06,323 --> 00:52:07,691
Right now, I'm…

880
00:52:08,459 --> 00:52:10,361
Run!

881
00:52:12,997 --> 00:52:15,099
Stop right there!

882
00:52:15,165 --> 00:52:17,201
Stop right there! Hey!

883
00:52:17,968 --> 00:52:21,005
In there, go that way! In there!

884
00:52:27,077 --> 00:52:28,746
Turn around, damn it!

885
00:52:28,812 --> 00:52:31,215
Grandpa! Grandpa, stop those guys!

886
00:52:31,281 --> 00:52:33,651
They're Man-gu's ginseng field thieves!

887
00:52:33,717 --> 00:52:35,185
Huh? Oh, thieves?

888
00:52:37,187 --> 00:52:39,289
-Stop, you punks!
-Get them!

889
00:52:39,356 --> 00:52:42,026
Who's this old man?
Move, or you'll get hurt!

890
00:52:44,328 --> 00:52:46,530
Oh no, my chocolate bars.

891
00:52:48,332 --> 00:52:50,668
These rascals cannot be forgiven.

892
00:52:51,435 --> 00:52:53,237
What should we do?

893
00:52:56,607 --> 00:52:59,877
Hup, ho, hup, ho.

894
00:52:59,943 --> 00:53:01,578
Do you want to die, old man?

895
00:53:04,848 --> 00:53:06,617
Why, you old geezer!

896
00:53:09,019 --> 00:53:11,822
Hup, ho, hup.

897
00:53:11,889 --> 00:53:13,824
Who is your grandpa, really?

898
00:53:14,958 --> 00:53:17,461
My grandpa is a Taekkyeon master.

899
00:53:17,528 --> 00:53:19,430
They messed with the wrong guy.

900
00:53:24,068 --> 00:53:27,771
Gosh, they stole so much.
These goddamn bastards!

901
00:53:28,739 --> 00:53:31,475
This is my ginseng! You bastards!

902
00:53:31,542 --> 00:53:33,877
You're all dead meat today!

903
00:53:33,944 --> 00:53:36,313
Please stop this, all of you.

904
00:53:36,380 --> 00:53:38,348
We will handle the punishment…

905
00:53:38,415 --> 00:53:40,651
Thanks for earlier, Sang-deuk.

906
00:53:40,718 --> 00:53:42,219
Forget it.

907
00:53:43,087 --> 00:53:46,924
This happens because you go around
flashing your smile like that.

908
00:53:56,834 --> 00:54:00,637
Wow, the view is so nice, isn't it?

909
00:54:01,638 --> 00:54:03,774
Wow, look at this tree! It's huge!

910
00:54:03,841 --> 00:54:05,642
It's pretty.

911
00:54:05,709 --> 00:54:08,312
They're taking photos.
Should we take one too?

912
00:54:08,378 --> 00:54:09,980
Careful, careful, careful.

913
00:54:10,047 --> 00:54:12,349
Let's go take a photo. Come on, hurry!

914
00:54:14,818 --> 00:54:15,886
-Look.
-Is it good?

915
00:54:17,221 --> 00:54:19,156
Hi, could you take our photo?

916
00:54:19,223 --> 00:54:20,991
-Sure.
-Thank you.

917
00:54:24,361 --> 00:54:25,662
Okay, taking it now.

918
00:54:25,729 --> 00:54:28,799
One, two, three.

919
00:54:28,866 --> 00:54:31,702
Please take just one more. Just one.

920
00:54:31,769 --> 00:54:35,038
Okay, taking it now. One, two, three.

921
00:54:35,105 --> 00:54:37,040
-It turned out well.
-Thank you.

922
00:54:37,107 --> 00:54:38,208
-Thank you.
-Sure.

923
00:54:40,110 --> 00:54:43,914
Wow, amazing! You look so gorgeous!

924
00:54:44,481 --> 00:54:46,016
How can you be so pretty?

925
00:54:46,083 --> 00:54:48,619
How long do I have to
get dragged around? Jeez.

926
00:54:48,685 --> 00:54:50,988
I just want to dump him and go rest.

927
00:54:51,922 --> 00:54:54,291
But he even cracked his skull for me,

928
00:54:54,358 --> 00:54:56,794
so I can't do that. I'm going crazy!

929
00:54:57,628 --> 00:55:00,664
Fine. I feel bad, but let's tell him.

930
00:55:00,731 --> 00:55:03,967
Um, Han-cheol,
I really have something to tell you.

931
00:55:04,034 --> 00:55:05,736
What do you keep trying to say?

932
00:55:05,803 --> 00:55:07,070
Please, go ahead.

933
00:55:08,438 --> 00:55:10,340
Wow, amazing. She's so pretty.

934
00:55:10,407 --> 00:55:13,710
Look, Han-cheol, I told you
I really have something to say!

935
00:55:21,952 --> 00:55:23,120
Han-cheol!

936
00:55:32,029 --> 00:55:33,697
Are you okay, Han-cheol?

937
00:55:44,141 --> 00:55:46,910
Han-cheol, pull yourself together!

938
00:55:48,445 --> 00:55:50,447
I'm okay, Su-yeon.

939
00:55:50,514 --> 00:55:52,182
What do you mean you're okay?

940
00:55:52,249 --> 00:55:54,651
You could die, so stay still.

941
00:55:54,718 --> 00:55:57,487
He could die?

942
00:55:57,554 --> 00:55:58,589
Ever see the news?

943
00:55:58,655 --> 00:56:00,891
Hornet venom is extremely toxic.

944
00:56:00,958 --> 00:56:02,826
-He needs a hospital now.
-Wait!

945
00:56:03,527 --> 00:56:05,462
-Hold on.
-Why, why, why?

946
00:56:07,998 --> 00:56:09,733
Su-yeon.

947
00:56:09,800 --> 00:56:11,401
I have something to tell you.

948
00:56:11,468 --> 00:56:13,804
Tell her later! Every second counts!

949
00:56:13,871 --> 00:56:15,873
No, it cannot wait. It cannot wait.

950
00:56:15,939 --> 00:56:19,977
While I still remain conscious,
I must hear your answer without fail.

951
00:56:20,043 --> 00:56:21,345
Make it quick, then.

952
00:56:22,112 --> 00:56:25,182
Su-yeon, I love you.

953
00:56:27,084 --> 00:56:29,186
-What?
-Please give me a chance.

954
00:56:30,354 --> 00:56:31,989
Could you accept my feelings?

955
00:56:32,055 --> 00:56:34,858
I'll make you happy.

956
00:56:36,894 --> 00:56:39,830
His eyes are rolling back!
Load him up! Hurry, hurry!

957
00:56:39,897 --> 00:56:42,566
No! No, I…

958
00:56:44,034 --> 00:56:45,636
I must hear her answer first.

959
00:56:45,702 --> 00:56:48,739
Miss, answer him quickly!
He'll die at this rate!

960
00:56:50,507 --> 00:56:53,677
Jeez, fine, let's date!
Let's just date, okay?

961
00:56:54,845 --> 00:56:57,047
Really? You mean it?

962
00:56:57,114 --> 00:56:58,615
Yes, hurry and get in.

963
00:57:05,222 --> 00:57:07,791
Then starting today,

964
00:57:10,294 --> 00:57:12,763
it's our day one as a couple.

965
00:57:18,669 --> 00:57:21,772
What will that kid do,
being such a bad drunk already?

966
00:57:21,838 --> 00:57:23,440
Gosh.

967
00:57:26,576 --> 00:57:28,445
Is she not here yet?

968
00:57:33,116 --> 00:57:35,052
Hi there.

969
00:57:35,118 --> 00:57:37,387
You must be Mi-yeong's daughter.

970
00:57:38,722 --> 00:57:40,624
You're so pretty.

971
00:57:40,691 --> 00:57:41,792
What's your name?

972
00:57:41,858 --> 00:57:44,895
When asking for someone's name,
giving yours first

973
00:57:44,962 --> 00:57:45,896
is polite, right?

974
00:57:45,963 --> 00:57:47,331
Huh?

975
00:57:47,397 --> 00:57:49,933
Right, sorry, sorry.

976
00:57:50,000 --> 00:57:52,202
My name is Park Sang-deuk.

977
00:57:52,269 --> 00:57:53,236
And what's yours?

978
00:57:53,303 --> 00:57:55,939
Don't you know it's rude
to ask a lady her name?

979
00:57:56,974 --> 00:57:58,842
Is that so? I'm sorry.

980
00:57:58,909 --> 00:58:01,845
By the way, who are you, mister?

981
00:58:01,912 --> 00:58:03,814
Me?

982
00:58:03,880 --> 00:58:05,983
The man who could've been your dad.

983
00:58:06,750 --> 00:58:07,884
Your mom's friend.

984
00:58:07,951 --> 00:58:10,554
Did you and Mom have
a flirtationship back then?

985
00:58:10,620 --> 00:58:12,589
Flirtationship? What's that?

986
00:58:12,656 --> 00:58:14,725
You're so out of touch. Forget it.

987
00:58:18,895 --> 00:58:21,064
She's so aloof, just like her mom.

988
00:58:23,734 --> 00:58:26,403
Sang-deuk, what are you doing here?

989
00:58:27,004 --> 00:58:29,072
I just stopped by on my way past.

990
00:58:30,107 --> 00:58:32,075
Why? Something you want to tell me?

991
00:58:32,142 --> 00:58:33,477
It's nothing special.

992
00:58:34,611 --> 00:58:36,146
Here.

993
00:58:37,614 --> 00:58:40,384
-What's this?
-A grand opening gift.

994
00:58:40,450 --> 00:58:43,487
We're old neighbors,
so I couldn't just do nothing.

995
00:58:45,122 --> 00:58:47,424
You didn't have to buy this.

996
00:58:48,959 --> 00:58:51,094
What is this?

997
00:58:51,762 --> 00:58:53,630
If obnoxious jerks show up again,

998
00:58:53,697 --> 00:58:54,564
just spray them.

999
00:58:54,631 --> 00:58:56,266
It'll blind them for a while.

1000
00:58:56,333 --> 00:58:59,936
Then just blast that whatchamacallit.

1001
00:59:00,003 --> 00:59:01,538
-Got that?
-What?

1002
00:59:01,605 --> 00:59:05,542
I just worry about you like a sister,
so don't get the wrong idea.

1003
00:59:20,223 --> 00:59:22,726
Su-yeon, please walk a little slower.

1004
00:59:22,793 --> 00:59:23,894
I'm a patient, okay?

1005
00:59:27,431 --> 00:59:31,768
I told you to just go inside and rest.
Why are you being so stubborn?

1006
00:59:31,835 --> 00:59:35,972
Still, I have to escort you home.

1007
00:59:36,039 --> 00:59:38,708
It's basic courtesy to my girlfriend.

1008
00:59:41,778 --> 00:59:44,214
We're here now, so go back and rest.

1009
00:59:45,615 --> 00:59:47,517
Su-yeon.

1010
00:59:47,584 --> 00:59:51,021
Thank you for accepting my feelings.

1011
00:59:52,355 --> 00:59:55,025
Okay, I know.

1012
00:59:55,092 --> 00:59:56,259
Su-yeon.

1013
00:59:57,828 --> 00:59:59,429
What now? What is it?

1014
00:59:59,496 --> 01:00:01,631
Let's meet

1015
01:00:01,698 --> 01:00:04,334
in our dreams.

1016
01:00:16,279 --> 01:00:19,349
Have some sweet potatoes with kimchi.

1017
01:00:27,991 --> 01:00:30,660
Jeez, this is driving me crazy.

1018
01:00:31,628 --> 01:00:33,697
I just dug myself into a deeper hole.

1019
01:00:35,132 --> 01:00:38,435
That guy raised his hand
like this to hit Yun-hui.

1020
01:00:38,502 --> 01:00:40,370
So I charged right at him.

1021
01:00:40,437 --> 01:00:42,739
But then, wow!

1022
01:00:42,806 --> 01:00:45,442
I'd seen those eyes somewhere before.

1023
01:00:45,509 --> 01:00:47,677
But his eyes were pretty.

1024
01:00:47,744 --> 01:00:50,413
So pretty, way too pretty.

1025
01:00:50,480 --> 01:00:53,283
Right then, bam, it hit me.

1026
01:00:53,350 --> 01:00:56,953
Whoa, these eyes are those eyes.

1027
01:00:57,721 --> 01:01:00,557
These eyes are that thief's eyes.

1028
01:01:01,758 --> 01:01:04,261
Then wee-woo, pow, pow, clink, clink!

1029
01:01:05,362 --> 01:01:07,831
Grandpa caught all the thieves himself.

1030
01:01:07,898 --> 01:01:10,534
You just twiddled your thumbs.
Quit bragging.

1031
01:01:11,301 --> 01:01:13,470
Still, without me,
who'd know it was them?

1032
01:01:13,537 --> 01:01:15,906
All right, you did a great job.

1033
01:01:15,972 --> 01:01:19,376
Since you did a great job,
I'll make something tasty tonight.

1034
01:01:19,442 --> 01:01:21,077
What would you like to eat?

1035
01:01:21,611 --> 01:01:23,280
Spaghetti?

1036
01:01:23,346 --> 01:01:25,048
Spaghetti? Okay.

1037
01:01:25,115 --> 01:01:26,883
Oh, yes!

1038
01:01:33,056 --> 01:01:35,091
No, not spaghetti.

1039
01:01:35,158 --> 01:01:37,060
Not spaghetti at all.

1040
01:01:37,127 --> 01:01:40,330
I think this canned food
you always set out for us

1041
01:01:40,397 --> 01:01:43,033
tastes the best in the world, yes.

1042
01:01:43,934 --> 01:01:45,869
Does he like spaghetti that much?

1043
01:01:46,436 --> 01:01:48,038
Having lunch, I see?

1044
01:01:48,104 --> 01:01:49,339
-Welcome.
-Hello.

1045
01:01:49,406 --> 01:01:50,874
You're here, ma'am.

1046
01:01:50,941 --> 01:01:52,676
You came too, Hwa-ran.

1047
01:01:52,742 --> 01:01:55,011
Take a photo of Hwa-ran for me.

1048
01:01:55,078 --> 01:01:56,713
You have a good camera here.

1049
01:01:56,780 --> 01:01:58,815
Why a photo all of a sudden?

1050
01:01:58,882 --> 01:02:02,319
Hwa-ran's mom in Yanbian
has a birthday in a few days.

1051
01:02:02,385 --> 01:02:04,254
Her mom asked her to send a photo.

1052
01:02:04,321 --> 01:02:06,256
Okay, got it.

1053
01:02:06,323 --> 01:02:08,825
I'll take a really pretty photo of you.

1054
01:02:08,892 --> 01:02:11,728
But if she sends a photo like that,

1055
01:02:11,795 --> 01:02:14,297
won't they think
their daughter became a ghost?

1056
01:02:14,364 --> 01:02:16,533
You're right, we can't have that.

1057
01:02:16,600 --> 01:02:18,635
-Hwa-ran?
-Yes?

1058
01:02:19,302 --> 01:02:21,905
Come with me.

1059
01:02:21,972 --> 01:02:24,374
Let's go. I'll give you a makeover.

1060
01:02:24,441 --> 01:02:27,611
As if a makeover could save her looks.

1061
01:02:30,647 --> 01:02:33,049
All right, everyone, get ready!

1062
01:02:33,116 --> 01:02:35,685
Hwa-ran, come on out.

1063
01:02:39,256 --> 01:02:42,392
Wow! Is that really Hwa-ran?

1064
01:02:42,459 --> 01:02:44,794
Lucky you, Ki-jun.

1065
01:02:44,861 --> 01:02:46,730
Your wife is gorgeous.

1066
01:02:47,430 --> 01:02:51,568
Uh… Stop calling her my wife already.

1067
01:02:53,503 --> 01:02:56,039
But she's pretty. She's so pretty.

1068
01:02:56,973 --> 01:02:59,276
My goodness.

1069
01:02:59,342 --> 01:03:01,411
She's so pretty dressed up like that.

1070
01:03:01,478 --> 01:03:03,213
Why'd she go around like that?

1071
01:03:03,280 --> 01:03:04,881
Unbelievable.

1072
01:03:04,948 --> 01:03:08,685
Hwa-ran, come sit right over here.

1073
01:03:11,254 --> 01:03:13,323
Okay, say cheese.

1074
01:03:15,191 --> 01:03:16,860
What, is this a mug shot?

1075
01:03:16,926 --> 01:03:19,296
Give me a nice, bright smile.

1076
01:03:19,996 --> 01:03:23,667
Did your face freeze up like a mouse?
Should I call a cat?

1077
01:03:23,733 --> 01:03:25,835
Oh, that's great! Hold on, hold on!

1078
01:03:28,004 --> 01:03:31,074
Oh my goodness, you look so pretty.

1079
01:03:31,141 --> 01:03:32,942
Any shot's like a magazine shoot.

1080
01:03:36,513 --> 01:03:38,381
She's even prettier when she smiles.

1081
01:03:39,316 --> 01:03:42,085
So pretty I can't tell
if she's a flower or a person.

1082
01:03:44,054 --> 01:03:44,954
Hwa-ran's groom!

1083
01:03:45,021 --> 01:03:47,357
Hurry over by her
and take one as a couple.

1084
01:03:47,424 --> 01:03:49,392
Wait… Why me? Why?

1085
01:03:49,459 --> 01:03:50,860
Yes, that's a great idea.

1086
01:03:50,927 --> 01:03:52,929
-Hurry on over.
-Just take one photo.

1087
01:03:52,996 --> 01:03:54,931
Just take one already.

1088
01:03:54,998 --> 01:03:56,533
Seeing a photo of you two

1089
01:03:56,599 --> 01:03:58,268
making friends and doing well,

1090
01:03:58,335 --> 01:04:00,003
Hwa-ran's mom will be so happy.

1091
01:04:00,070 --> 01:04:02,772
That's right. Both of you, look here.

1092
01:04:02,839 --> 01:04:04,741
Oh my, seeing you two sit together,

1093
01:04:04,808 --> 01:04:07,410
you really look like a couple.

1094
01:04:08,345 --> 01:04:10,947
What's this?
Why is my heart racing like this?

1095
01:04:11,014 --> 01:04:13,316
Why am I like this? Why on earth?
